# Copy these into Railway > your service > Variables. Nothing here is needed to RUN the site; only the first block is recommended.

# --- recommended ---
NODE_ENV=production
# Railway sets PORT for you. If you attached a Volume, Railway also sets RAILWAY_VOLUME_MOUNT_PATH and the server uses it automatically.
# DATA_DIR=/data                      # only if you want to choose the folder yourself

# --- camera scanners (AI Food + Ingredients). Without a provider the camera still opens; analysing says "not switched on for this site yet". ---
# Default provider = Anthropic (the keys you already have keep working):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# SCAN_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5          # optional (VISION_MODEL does the same and wins if both are set)
# Optional tuning (all have safe defaults):
# VISION_TIMEOUT_MS=45000              # how long to wait for the provider before telling the user it timed out
# SCAN_DAILY_LIMIT=20                  # photos per member per day (failed analyses are not counted)
# Any other provider or a self-hosted vision model that speaks the OpenAI "chat/completions" format with image input:
# VISION_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
# VISION_BASE_URL=https://your-provider.example/v1
# VISION_MODEL=your-vision-model-name
# VISION_API_KEY=                      # leave out for a self-hosted server without a key
# VISION_MAX_TOKENS=4000              # raise if a "thinking" model returns cut-off answers
# --- Google Gemini (native API, works with the new "AQ." keys) ---
# VISION_PROVIDER=gemini
# VISION_MODEL=<short model id from Google AI Studio, no spaces>
# VISION_API_KEY=<your Gemini API key>
# FDC_API_KEY=                         # free key from api.data.gov, for nutrition numbers (not related to photo recognition)

# --- password reset by email (Resend). Without it "Forgot password" tells the user it is not set up. ---
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# MAIL_FROM=Simple Cook <no-reply@yourdomain.com>

# --- map ---
# MAP_STYLE_URL=https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/style.json?key=YOUR_KEY   # production map tiles (the default OSM demo tiles are for light use only)
# GEOCODER_URL=https://photon.komoot.io/api/
# OSM_PLACES=0                        # 0 = do not load restaurants from OpenStreetMap automatically
# PLACES_AUTO_APPROVE=0               # 0 = new places wait for you (node server/admin.js approve-place <id>); default: shown immediately as "community-added"

# --- chatbot (Zapier) ---
# PUBLIC_CHATBOT_URL=https://simple-cook-bot.zapier.app
# PUBLIC_CHATBOT_EMBED_URL=
